entry.summary:
The Problem


When building post-campaign influencer monitoring for Indian D2C brands at PulseROI, cron jobs fetching live YouTube creator engagement metrics hit Vercel's 300-second serverless execution limit and time out halfway through processing 50+ active creator profiles.
My initial approach was a straightforward sequential for...of loop running inside a Next.js API route triggered by cron-job.org:
// The naive approach that timed out on creator #23
export async function GET(req: Request) {
  const creators = await db.query('SELECT * FROM active_creators');

  for (const creator of creators) {
    // Each YouTube Data API v3 call takes ~800ms to 1.5s
    const metrics = await fetchYouTubeMetrics(creator.channel_id);
    await db.query('UPDATE creators SET stats = $1 WHERE id = $2', [m…
